===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰreg-}}
From {{der|en|fr|refrain}}, from the {{der|en|fro|-}} verb {{m|fro|refraindre|t=to break off, repeat}}, from {{der|en|la|re-|t=back, again}} + {{m|la|frangō|t=break}}; compare {{cog|oc|refranhs|t=a refrain}}, {{m|oc|refranher|t=to repeat}}. See {{m|en|refract}} and the verb {{m|en|refrain}}.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# The [[chorus]] or {{l|en|burden|id=music}} of a [[song]] [[repeat]]ed at the end of each [[verse]] or [[stanza]].
#* {{quote-book|en|chapter=1|title=Nineteen Eighty-Four|author=George Orwell|year=1949|passage=For perhaps as much as thirty seconds they kept it up. It was a '''refrain''' that was often heard in moments of overwhelming emotion. Partly it was a sort of hymn to the wisdom and majesty of Big Brother, but still more it was an act of self-hypnosis, a deliberate drowning of consciousness by means of rhythmic noise.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A much repeated [[comment]], [[complaint]], or [[saying]].
#: {{syn|en|old saw}}

